course: dictionary
lesson: 4387
title: Haemoglobin, the blood's oxygen carrier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your blood is red because of a substance called haemoglobin. It sits inside red blood cells, and its job is to carry oxygen. Oxygen comes into your body through your lungs, and haemoglobin picks it up and carries it all around your body.
explain: The example says «Red blood cells carry oxygen using iron-rich haemoglobin». Use the context clues: the cells carry oxygen using haemoglobin, so haemoglobin is the tool that does the carrying. The words "iron-rich" tell you that haemoglobin contains iron.
explain: Your muscles need oxygen to work, so haemoglobin helps you run, jump and keep going. When someone looks pale and tired, a doctor may do a blood test to measure their haemoglobin.
fact: Haemoglobin is the red substance in red blood cells.
fact: It carries oxygen from the lungs around the body.
fact: It gives blood its red colour.
fact: Haemoglobin contains iron, so iron-rich foods such as beans, spinach and red meat help keep it healthy.
fact: Doctors measure haemoglobin in blood tests; too little can cause anaemia, which makes people tired and pale.
exercise: «Red blood cells carry oxygen using iron-rich haemoglobin.» What does haemoglobin carry? | Blood platelets | Sugar | Germs | *Oxygen
exercise: Which food helps keep haemoglobin healthy? | Fizzy drinks | *Spinach | Crisps | Sweets
exercise: Why is blood red? | Because of white cells | *Because of haemoglobin in red blood cells | Because of the heart beating | Because of platelets fighting germs
test: What does too little haemoglobin, or anaemia, make people feel? | Full of energy | Extremely loud | Very hot and sweaty | *Tired and pale
test: Where does haemoglobin pick up oxygen? | In the feet | In the stomach | In the ears | *In the lungs
exam: A blood test shows «low haemoglobin». What does this mean? | The person has just eaten a big meal | The blood has too many germs | *There is too little haemoglobin in the blood, which may lead to anaemia | The heart has stopped beating
